Revision history for XARF

1.00  2026-04-01
    - Initial release (XARF spec v4.2.0)
    - Parser: parse() accepts JSON strings and hashrefs; supports strict mode
      and show_missing_optional; auto-detects and converts XARF v3 reports
    - Generator: create_report() builds validated reports with auto-generated
      xarf_version, report_id (UUID v4), and timestamp (ISO 8601)
    - Evidence: create_evidence() with automatic base64 encoding, hashing
      (sha256 default; sha512/sha1/md5 supported), and size calculation
    - Schema-driven validation via JSON::Schema::Modern (Draft 2020-12)
    - Supports all 7 abuse categories (messaging, connection, content,
      infrastructure, copyright, vulnerability, reputation) and all 32 report
      types defined by the specification
    - XARF::SchemaRegistry singleton: schema-derived category/type introspection
      and field metadata without hardcoded rules
    - v3 backward compatibility with automatic conversion and deprecation
      warnings (XARF::V3Legacy)
    - Bundled schemas shipped as File::ShareDir share files; xarf-fetch-schemas
      installed CLI to pull updated schemas from xarf-spec
    - Result objects (XARF::Result::Parse, XARF::Result::CreateReport) with
      structured errors, warnings, and optional info list
    - Complete exception hierarchy: XARF::Error, XARF::ParseError,
      XARF::ValidationError, XARF::SchemaError
